475 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 327 0 R
/E (Guaranteeing exact proportions on three dimensions at once \(homeownership, parental status, and region\) is already a fine-grained calculation. Adding more characteristics as formal quotas, such as race, gender, income, urban/suburban/rural residence, and political party, would have required subdividing the enrollee pool into 1,728 separate categories, most of which would have too few people to fill reliably.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
476 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 327 0 R
/E (Instead, these five additional characteristics were balanced through a technique called rerandomization: after a panel was drawn using the procedure above, it was checked against Connecticut population benchmarks on:)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
