/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 331 0 R
/T (The system members ratified combined representative and direct-democracy elements proposed by the organizers. A seven-member executive committee, drawn by lottery and rotating members every session, was empowered to handle procedural and governance matters on the Assembly's behalf between full votes; rotating rapporteurs initially accompanied the committee to help relay discussion back to the full group. Because the seven turned over each session, no small group could accumulate lasting procedural power. As a direct-democracy safeguard, any individual member could bring a question directly to the seven, and any bloc of ten or more members could force a floor motion to a vote of the full 100-person Assembly, bypassing the committee if members felt it necessary.)
/E (The system members ratified combined representative and direct-democracy elements proposed by the organizers. A seven-member executive committee, drawn by lottery and rotating members every session, was empowered to handle procedural and governance matters on the Assembly's behalf between full votes; rotating rapporteurs initially accompanied the committee to help relay discussion back to the full group. Because the seven turned over each session, no small group could accumulate lasting procedural power. As a direct-democracy safeguard, any individual member could bring a question directly to the seven, and any bloc of ten or more members could force a floor motion to a vote of the full 100-person Assembly, bypassing the committee if members felt it necessary.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [2]
>>
