746 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 338 0 R
/T (By 2028, a dedicated state commission should be established with the authority to enact school district regionalization policies and adopt a comprehensive implementation plan for the upcoming legislative session. District consolidation offers significant opportunities to advance educational equity across the state and capture economies of scale in transportation, purchasing, and other back-office functions, including unified payroll and expense management. While this transition requires municipalities to relinquish specific local autonomy regarding elected school boards and executive hiring, the resulting cost savings can directly fund classroom improvements, expand student educational programs, and support local tax reductions.)
/E (By 2028, a dedicated state commission should be established with the authority to enact school district regionalization policies and adopt a comprehensive implementation plan for the upcoming legislative session. District consolidation offers significant opportunities to advance educational equity across the state and capture economies of scale in transportation, purchasing, and other back-office functions, including unified payroll and expense management. While this transition requires municipalities to relinquish specific local autonomy regarding elected school boards and executive hiring, the resulting cost savings can directly fund classroom improvements, expand student educational programs, and support local tax reductions.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
747 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 338 0 R
/T (To facilitate a smooth transition, the state should fully fund fiscal impact analyses and conduct regional workforce studies to evaluate effects on union personnel. The regionalization process should be streamlined by adopting a staggered implementation model that merges educational levels incrementally rather than all at once. Furthermore, state statutes should be amended to prevent the complete dissolution of a regionalization agreement if a single participating municipality withdraws.)
/E (To facilitate a smooth transition, the state should fully fund fiscal impact analyses and conduct regional workforce studies to evaluate effects on union personnel. The regionalization process should be streamlined by adopting a staggered implementation model that merges educational levels incrementally rather than all at once. Furthermore, state statutes should be amended to prevent the complete dissolution of a regionalization agreement if a single participating municipality withdraws.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [9]
>>
