/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 342 0 R
/T (Restaurant sales tax \(the 1% portion\): The revenue from the 1% portion of the sales tax on meals and beverages would be divided equally. Half would go to the State Tourism Fund, to keep investing in the visitor economy that generates this revenue. The other half would go to the municipality where the sale took place, dedicated to public safety and public works. This mirrors the meals tax provision of Substitute Senate Bill 2 \(2026 session, File No. 693\), which received a favorable report from the Finance, Revenue and Bonding Committee and was supported by the Connecticut Conference of Municipalities, the Connecticut Business and Industry Association, and the restaurant, hospitality and tourism industries.)
/E (Restaurant sales tax \(the 1% portion\): The revenue from the 1% portion of the sales tax on meals and beverages would be divided equally. Half would go to the State Tourism Fund, to keep investing in the visitor economy that generates this revenue. The other half would go to the municipality where the sale took place, dedicated to public safety and public works. This mirrors the meals tax provision of Substitute Senate Bill 2 \(2026 session, File No. 693\), which received a favorable report from the Finance, Revenue and Bonding Committee and was supported by the Connecticut Conference of Municipalities, the Connecticut Business and Industry Association, and the restaurant, hospitality and tourism industries.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [0]
