/P 342 0 R
/T ( How this reduces property taxes: Police, fire, emergency response and road maintenance are among the largest costs in every municipal budget and are funded today almost entirely by local property taxpayers. Restaurants and hotels add to those costs by bringing in patrons who live elsewhere. Dedicating a share of the revenue those patrons generate to the services they use lowers the amount each municipality must raise through the property tax.)
/E ( How this reduces property taxes: Police, fire, emergency response and road maintenance are among the largest costs in every municipal budget and are funded today almost entirely by local property taxpayers. Restaurants and hotels add to those costs by bringing in patrons who live elsewhere. Dedicating a share of the revenue those patrons generate to the services they use lowers the amount each municipality must raise through the property tax.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
790 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 342 0 R
/T (What would need to change: Implementation requires legislation directing the Department of Revenue Services to distribute the municipal shares based on where the tax is collected. The legislation would restrict the municipal share to public safety and public works, and would require each municipality to report annually on how the funds were used. No new collection system is needed, because both taxes are already collected and remitted by location.)
/E (What would need to change: Implementation requires legislation directing the Department of Revenue Services to distribute the municipal shares based on where the tax is collected. The legislation would restrict the municipal share to public safety and public works, and would require each municipality to report annually on how the funds were used. No new collection system is needed, because both taxes are already collected and remitted by location.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
791 0 obj
