/T (A barrier is that no funding source currently exists for this program. The state will have to create a new funding source and distribute funding based on need, which may be viewed by some as relinquishing local control. The plan may involve redistribution of the tax burden that may increase total taxes for some. The plan is likely to decrease the risk of sudden cost increases for municipalities based on unforeseen special education needs. Fiscally predictable and timely funds may decrease special education costs over time because it ensures earlier intervention. Centralized \(state\) funding could create future purchasing power efficiency. )
