/T (As Connecticut municipalities rely heavily on local property taxes to fund essential public services, top-down state mandates place an unsustainable financial burden directly onto local homeowners and businesses. Currently, the state legislature can pass sweeping  laws that force towns to expand services, increase expenditures, or hire specialized personnel without providing sufficient state revenue to cover those costs or adequate feedback mechanisms.)
/E (As Connecticut municipalities rely heavily on local property taxes to fund essential public services, top-down state mandates place an unsustainable financial burden directly onto local homeowners and businesses. Currently, the state legislature can pass sweeping  laws that force towns to expand services, increase expenditures, or hire specialized personnel without providing sufficient state revenue to cover those costs or adequate feedback mechanisms.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
