/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 352 0 R
/E (A 2023 state analysis estimated that interstate tolls could generate approximately $950 million annually, with roughly 40% of that revenue coming from out-of-state drivers. The total projected toll revenue is comparable to the amount Connecticut municipalities collect annually through the motor vehicle property tax, demonstrating the potential scale of the revenue source. )
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
912 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 352 0 R
/E (Q2. How does this proposal directly address the problem above? What mechanisms or policies would need to be created or changed to implement this proposal?)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
913 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 352 0 R
/E (Under federal requirements, toll revenue generally must be used for eligible transportation purposes and could not simply be redirected to property tax relief. This proposal would address that limitation by using toll revenue to fund eligible Connecticut Department of Transportation expenses, thereby reducing the amount of other state revenue needed to support those expenses. The legislature could then dedicate an equivalent amount of state revenue to property tax relief, including potential relief from the motor vehicle property tax.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
914 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 352 0 R
/E (Implementation would require authorization of interstate tolling, federal review and approval as applicable, and investment in electronic tolling infrastructure and related technology. Legislation would also need to establish a dedicated mechanism to ensure that the state revenue made available through tolling is directed specifically toward property tax relief.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
915 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 352 0 R
/E (To ensure transparency and accountability, the proposal would require an annual public audit detailing toll revenue collected, allowable transportation expenditures funded by that revenue, administrative and operating costs, and the corresponding state funds dedicated to property tax relief. Any eligible costs associated with administering the tolling system would be paid from toll revenue to the extent permitted under federal law.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
