<<
/Title (ownership, family ties, and social networks. Neighboring states like Massachusetts, New York, and New Jersey have already successfully passed high-earner tax reforms without destroying their tax bases; a Connecticut Fair Share Act simply aligns CT with its regional peers. Even if a tiny fraction of high earners choose to relocate, the massive revenue generated by the remaining 99% of millionaires vastly eclipses any minor loss, providing the critical funds needed to lower local property taxes for everyone else.)
/Dest [39 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1923 0 R
