2638 0 obj
<<
/Title (By 2028, a dedicated state commission should be established with the authority to enact school district regionalization policies and adopt a comprehensive implementation plan for the upcoming legislative session. District consolidation offers significant opportunities to advance educational equity across the state and capture economies of scale in transportation, purchasing, and other back-office functions, including unified payroll and expense management. While this transition requires municipalities to relinquish specific local autonomy regarding elected school boards and executive hiring, the resulting cost savings can directly fund classroom improvements, expand student educational programs, and support local tax reductions.)
/Dest [26 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2613 0 R
/Next 2639 0 R
>>
endobj
2639 0 obj
<<
/Title (To facilitate a smooth transition, the state should fully fund fiscal impact analyses and conduct regional workforce studies to evaluate effects on union personnel. The regionalization process should be streamlined by adopting a staggered implementation model that merges educational levels incrementally rather than all at once. Furthermore, state statutes should be amended to prevent the complete dissolution of a regionalization agreement if a single participating municipality withdraws.)
/Dest [26 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2613 0 R
/Prev 2638 0 R
>>
endobj
2640 0 obj
<<
/Title (Volatility: Restaurant and hotel revenue rises and falls with the economy. Occupancy tax collections fell about 40% between FY 2019 and FY 2021, so municipalities would need to budget this revenue conservatively.)
/Dest [31 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2503 0 R
/Prev 2615 0 R
/Next 2641 0 R
>>
endobj
