/Title (This recommendation addresses the timing problem of state mandates that force municipalities to cover new costs mid-budget cycle. Legislation passed late in a session or with an earlier specified effective date can impose costs that are implemented during an already-adopted or nearly-adopted budget year, forcing mid-year adjustments, use of fund balances, service cuts, or property-tax increases that were not planned when the budget and mill rate were set.)
